.\" custom-claude-endpoint.conf(5) -- a custom API endpoint for Claude Code.
.\" @AI_TOOLS_VERSION@ is substituted at deploy time (install.sh install_subst
.\" and the RPM %prep), like ai-tools(1). The validation described here is the
.\" one claude-endpoint.lib.sh applies in the session-env fragment.
.TH CUSTOM-CLAUDE-ENDPOINT.CONF 5 "" "ai-tools @AI_TOOLS_VERSION@" "Agent Tools Restricted"
.SH NAME
custom-claude-endpoint.conf \- route sandboxed Claude Code sessions at a custom API endpoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/ai-tools/endpoints/custom-claude-endpoint.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
An endpoint file routes every Claude Code session on the host at an
Anthropic-compatible API other than the default one: a local proxy, or a
gateway of your own.
It is read only where
.BR operator.conf (5)
sets
.B CLAUDE_BASE_URL_FILE
to its path, and the shipped file is inert, every option commented, so
setting the pointer alone leaves the launch unchanged.
.PP
The file holds a credential, so it is owned by
.B root
in group
.B ai-tools
at mode
.BR 0640 :
root and the sandbox account read it, and no other account does.
Edit it with
.BR sudo .
The pointer in
.BR operator.conf (5)
is world-readable and holds only the path.
.PP
A file elsewhere is refused.
The path must resolve under
.IR /etc/ai-tools/endpoints/ ,
the one directory the confined session is granted read on, and the file,
that directory and
.BR operator.conf (5)
must each be root-owned and not group- or other-writable.
.PP
Only the four options below are read; any other key in the file is
ignored.
Each set option is validated when a session launches, and a set option that
is invalid
.B refuses the launch
rather than routing the session at a partial endpoint.
A file with every option commented leaves the environment as it is, and the
session launches at the default endpoint.
.PP
The file is parsed with the grammar
.BR operator.conf (5)
describes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL= url
The endpoint.
An
.B http://
or
.B https://
URL with no whitespace.
Required: another option set without it refuses the launch, since alone it
would only mis-route the default connection.
.TP
.BI ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN= token
The bearer token the endpoint expects, a single token with no whitespace.
It is passed to Claude Code by name, so its value does not appear on any
process command line.
An endpoint on
.BR localhost ,
.B 127.0.0.1
or
.B ::1
does not need one; for any other endpoint an absent token is reported
at launch and the session still starts.
.TP
.BI ANTHROPIC_MODEL= label
The model label the endpoint resolves, a single token.
With a proxy the label is whatever that proxy maps to an underlying model,
so it need not be an Anthropic model id.
.TP
.BI ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL= label
The label for the fast, background model, a single token.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The options become process environment variables of the session.
A Claude Code settings
.B env
block that sets the same name takes precedence, and
.I /etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json
is the host layer that takes precedence over a session's own settings.
The shipped settings set no
.B ANTHROPIC_*
key, so this file governs by default.
.PP
A running session may set these variables for itself or for a child
process; that does not repoint the client already started.
Where sessions may connect is decided by network policy, not by this file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ai-tools/endpoints/custom-claude-endpoint.conf
The shipped endpoint file, inert until edited.
.TP
.I /etc/ai-tools/endpoints/
The directory an endpoint file must live in.
A second file here is used by pointing
.B CLAUDE_BASE_URL_FILE
at it.
.SH EXAMPLES
A local proxy, which does not need a token:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder
.EE
.RE
.PP
A gateway that maps labels to an underlying model:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://chat.example.tld
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=replace-with-your-token
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
.EE
.RE
.PP
Point sessions at the file, in
.BR operator.conf (5):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
CLAUDE_BASE_URL_FILE=/etc/ai-tools/endpoints/custom-claude-endpoint.conf
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ai\-tools (1),
.BR operator.conf (5)
